                "text": "**Identifying Color Barriers**\n\nI've homed in on the \"grey\" color (5). It seems to act as a barrier. I'm noting where these grey blocks appear - in example one, it's a horizontal bar. In example two, it's a vertical one, and in the third, it's a double horizontal. I will see if that is consistent across all instances and how that may relate to other colors.\n\n\n**Analyzing Color Interactions**\n\nI've examined example one more closely. It seems the number of points on either side of the \"grey\" bar dictates the length of the \"5\" bar growth in the output. I am observing how this rule consistently applies to example two with the vertical \"grey\" bar. I'm verifying the same principle applies, but am still working through the implications of this rule.\n\n\n",
